{"w":2400,"h":3395,"lines":[{"h":0.014378241009931236,"c":1,"y":0.11296658201094134,"w":0.072624308268229187,"x":0.83511239189017528,"t":"Reading"},{"w":0.44855967203776043,"h":0.018941572613935254,"x":0.31893004041640588,"y":0.15547703164075055,"t":"Why companies should welcome disorder","c":1},{"w":0.70995483398437487,"y":0.18726435134368491,"t":"A Organisation is big business. Whether it is of our lives - all those inboxes and calendars -","h":0.015379354164653747,"x":0.17691999075841267,"c":1},{"h":0.016002068109590928,"c":1,"t":"or how companies are structured, a multi-billion dollar industry helps to meet this need.","x":0.21604939276497986,"y":0.20347467621497484,"w":0.65637858072916666},{"t":"We have more strategies for time management, project management and","h":0.013081395583944611,"y":0.22819767429840287,"x":0.2201646033042122,"w":0.53703704833984378,"c":1},{"y":0.24264113357959993,"w":0.64206334431966139,"x":0.21806403204450361,"h":0.01513954438927323,"c":1,"t":"self-organisation than at any other time in human history. We are told that we ought to"},{"y":0.25753089189151812,"w":0.67099177042643232,"t":"organise our company, our home life, our week, our day and even our sleep, all as a means","x":0.22006829462132885,"h":0.017146586248534823,"c":1},{"t":"to becoming more productive. Every week, countless seminars and workshops take place","y":0.27470930220518386,"h":0.013081395583944722,"w":0.66460906982421875,"x":0.218106987649619,"c":1},{"t":"around the world to tell a paying public that they ought to structure their lives in order to","y":0.28889446387795092,"c":1,"x":0.2180565699985389,"w":0.66059880574544261,"h":0.015933920272809043},{"y":0.32737648970472699,"w":0.66480143229166655,"t":"This rhetoric has also crept into the thinking of business leaders and entrepreneurs, much","x":0.21801704467093572,"h":0.018370940070270181,"c":1},{"y":0.34447674403929507,"t":"to the delight of self-proclaimed perfectionists with the need to get everything right. The","w":0.66255142211914075,"h":0.015988372380376759,"c":1,"x":0.2160493917379922},{"y":0.35843302392095899,"h":0.018816160509808277,"t":"number of business schools and graduates has massively increased over the past 50 years,","w":0.66885467529296871,"x":0.2180331795177608,"c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.21810699924681207,"y":0.37632508817779553,"h":0.01472320376914027,"w":0.36625513712565105,"t":"essentially teaching people how to organise well."},{"x":0.21394377108637494,"c":1,"y":0.39803535854121141,"h":0.01662724767893875,"t":"Ironically, however, the number of businesses that fail has also steadily increased.","w":0.61325775146484374},{"y":0.4133780613889142,"c":1,"t":"Work-related stress has increased. A large proportion of workers from all demographics","x":0.22011269799818137,"w":0.65239008585611979,"h":0.016553345220810645},{"x":0.21600375348076606,"y":0.42874211198831191,"h":0.017511162235543165,"c":1,"t":"claim to be dissatisfied with the way their work is structured and the way they are managed.","w":0.68526987711588538},{"y":0.45347467621388682,"x":0.21810699527854127,"h":0.016002068109590928,"c":1,"t":"This begs the question: what has gone wrong? Why is it that on paper the drive for","w":0.61522633870442711},{"y":0.46937573602734095,"w":0.66872426350911451,"x":0.22016461712499155,"t":"organisation seems a sure shot for increasing productivity, but in reality falls well short of","h":0.013250883392226021,"c":1},{"y":0.48546511613265575,"c":1,"x":0.21810699417382465,"w":0.13580247243245444,"t":"what is expected?","h":0.01453488398216074},{"c":1,"w":0.65432098388671878,"t":"This has been a problem for a while now. Frederick Taylor was one of the forefathers of","y":0.50872093011106423,"x":0.21810699775989822,"h":0.013081395583944611},{"x":0.21804285222480738,"w":0.66679433186848958,"t":"scientific management. Writing in the first half of the 20th century, he designed a number","h":0.017446873466033352,"c":1,"y":0.52318469988791261},{"x":0.21800353970479761,"y":0.53729288550282306,"c":1,"h":0.018661086775529245,"t":"of principles to improve the efficiency of the work process, which have since become","w":0.63395395914713548},{"c":1,"w":0.59670781453450528,"h":0.014555427856804748,"y":0.55523255800589144,"t":"widespread in modern companies. So the approach has been around for a while.","x":0.21810699799509317},{"h":0.017538527858271369,"c":1,"w":0.6832638041178386,"t":"New research suggests that this obsession with efficiency is misguided. The problem is not","x":0.21187397646185513,"y":0.57743641235115906},{"y":0.59149033146272989,"c":1,"x":0.22006904906118507,"h":0.018337397468665695,"t":"necessarily the management theories or strategies we use to organise our work; it's the basic","w":0.68332585652669275},{"t":"assumptions we hold in approaching how we work. Here it's the assumption that order is a","c":1,"w":0.6729529317220051,"x":0.21804974881567357,"h":0.017390572420980632,"y":0.60893491413566414},{"t":"necessary condition for productivity. This assumption has also fostered the idea that disorder","c":1,"h":0.014575971731448756,"y":0.6249999998644743,"x":0.21810699213385476,"w":0.69135803222656245},{"c":1,"h":0.015988372380376759,"y":0.63953488354764543,"w":0.6748971048990885,"t":"must be detrimental to organisational productivity. The result is that businesses and people","x":0.21810700411195549},{"c":1,"h":0.016423378170449254,"y":0.65547071033227422,"w":0.68528742472330728,"t":"spend time and money organising themselves for the sake of organising, rather than actually","x":0.22011085157973242},{"t":"looking at the end goal and usefulness of such an effort.","c":1,"x":0.22016460487141332,"y":0.67137809202535315,"h":0.014723203769140158,"w":0.41563786824544269},{"h":0.015927898308132793,"x":0.22012903848724988,"w":0.65852691650390627,"t":"What's more, recent studies show that order actually has diminishing returns. Order does","y":0.69461659649533147,"c":1},{"t":"increase productivity to a certain extent, but eventually the usefulness of the process of","x":0.22016461177631888,"y":0.71075581382056607,"h":0.01453488398216074,"c":1,"w":0.64814814249674479},{"x":0.22016460079265773,"y":0.72673733778133309,"w":0.66460906982421875,"h":0.013088243729374671,"c":1,"t":"organisation, and the benefit it yields, reduce until the point where any further increase in"},{"t":"order reduces productivity. Some argue that in a business, if the cost of formally structuring","y":0.73965588373269664,"w":0.68123942057291664,"h":0.017422557017547691,"c":1,"x":0.22008492843158592},{"c":1,"h":0.013081395583944722,"t":"something outweighs the benefit of doing it, then that thing ought not to be formally","x":0.22016459833290014,"w":0.62551442464192708,"y":0.75726744173945082},{"c":1,"x":0.22016462057612596,"t":"structured. Instead, the resources involved can be better used elsewhere.","y":0.77325581383284947,"w":0.53497940063476557,"h":0.013081395583944611},{"h":0.015988372380376759,"x":0.8827160489951833,"t":"47","w":0.026748971939086874,"c":1,"y":0.86627906950956246}]}